{%- comment -%}
  Which of the theme's collections have something to show, as ",handle,handle,".

  An empty collection is hidden everywhere it would appear — the home feed,
  categories, search, the app data — and comes back on its own as soon as it
  has an active (published) product again; no setting to flip.

  dedupe: true  — the home feed shows each product only under the first
                  collection that has it, so a collection whose products all
                  appeared earlier is empty *there* and is hidden too.

  Usage:
    {%- capture live -%}{% render 'live-collections', dedupe: true %}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign probe = ',' | append: c.handle | append: ',' -%}
    {%- if live contains probe -%} … {%- endif -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign seen = ',' -%}
{%- assign out = ',' -%}
{%- for c in settings.oka_collections -%}
  {%- assign n = 0 -%}
  {%- for p in c.products limit: 50 -%}
    {%- if dedupe -%}
      {%- assign probe = ',' | append: p.handle | append: ',' -%}
      {%- if seen contains probe -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- assign seen = seen | append: p.handle | append: ',' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- assign n = n | plus: 1 -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if n > 0 -%}{%- assign out = out | append: c.handle | append: ',' -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{- out -}}
